From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RChain-Axe <noreply@github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: support DS35M1GA on QPIC NAND controller

The DS35M1GA (raw ID e521e52100) exists in the Dosilicon chip table but
fails to probe on IPQ5018 QPIC NAND controller. QPIC reads chip ID via
hardware register rather than SPI command sequence, causing the
rdid_method check to reject the chip.

This patch:
1. Adds DS35M1GA entry with OPCODE_ONLY method (in case QPIC uses it)
2. Relaxed the method check so zero-method entries always match

---
 drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c    | 3 ++-
 drivers/mtd/nand/spi/dosilicon.c | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
@@ -1426,7 +1426,8 @@ int spinand_match_and_init(struct spinand
 	for (i = 0; i < table_size; i++) {
 		const struct spinand_info *info = &table[i];

-		if (rdid_method != info->devid.method)
+		/* QPIC reads ID via register; allow entries with method=0 */
+		if (info->devid.method && rdid_method != info->devid.method)
 			continue;

 		if (memcmp(id + 1, info->devid.id, min(3, info->devid.len)))
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/dosilicon.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/dosilicon.c
@@ -70,6 +70,17 @@ SPINAND_INFO("DS35Q1GA",
 		SPINAND_HAS_QE_BIT,
 		SPINAND_ECCINFO(&ds35xx_ooblayout, NULL)),
+
+	/* DS35M1GA as seen on QPIC (raw ID e5 21 e5 21 00) */
+	SPINAND_INFO("DS35M1GA-QPIC",
+		SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_ONLY, 0x21),
+		NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 64, 64, 1024, 20, 1, 1, 1),
+		NAND_ECCREQ(4, 512),
+		SPINAND_INFO_OP_VARIANTS(&read_cache_variants,
+					 &write_cache_variants,
+					 &update_cache_variants),
+		SPINAND_HAS_QE_BIT,
+		SPINAND_ECCINFO(&ds35xx_ooblayout, NULL)),
 	SPINAND_INFO("DS35M1GA",
 		SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_DUMMY, 0x21),
 		NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 64, 64, 1024, 20, 1, 1, 1),
